Package: parkeze-ap
Version: @VERSION@-@BUILD@
Depends: ucode, ucode-mod-uci, wpad-mbedtls, iw, dnsmasq-full, jsonfilter
Source: parkeze
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Joseph Telaak <joseph@parkeze.com>
Architecture: all
Description: Setup access point and captive portal.
 Raises a self-titled access point so a gateway can be reconfigured when it has
 dropped off the network, with a captive portal that joins a WiFi network or
 hands the unit back to LAN configuration. Open only while the gateway has no
 credentials to lose; WPA2 with a per-device key once it is adopted.
 .
 Depends on wpad rather than hostapd and wpa-supplicant separately: wpad IS
 both daemons in one binary and CONFLICTS with each of them, so asking for
 hostapd-basic-mbedtls alongside the wpad the boards already pull in is an
 unsatisfiable package set. This package needs AP mode and station mode, which
 is exactly what wpad provides.
 .
 The full wpad, not wpad-basic: basic has no 802.1X, so a gateway could not
 join WPA2-Enterprise (eduroam, most campus and corporate WiFi). mbedtls
 rather than openssl because it is the same size and needs no second TLS
 library, and its backend supports the probe:// and hash:// certificate
 handling parkeze-wifi-probe relies on.
